any2orca -- third-party data attribution

This file lists data any2orca's packages derive from or reference. It is not
legal advice; see each package's own LICENSE for the terms that apply to it.

## packages/profiles

The printer profile catalog is derived from preset data published by each
supported printer vendor's own OrcaSlicer-family fork (e.g. Snapmaker Orca,
github.com/Snapmaker/OrcaSlicer), which is itself AGPL-3.0-or-later. That
upstream provenance is why packages/profiles is AGPL-3.0-or-later rather than
MIT. See the Profiles section of each release's CHANGELOG.md for which
upstream release a given profile set tracks.

"Snapmaker," "OrcaSlicer," and other printer/slicer vendor names used in this
package are the trademarks of their respective owners. any2orca is an
independent project and is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by
any of them.

## Settings catalog (packages/core)

The names, settings-page locations, types, limits and choices of Snapmaker
Orca's settings (packages/core/src/diff/settingsCatalog.ts), used to label and
group settings, are generated from the setting definitions in Snapmaker Orca's
source (github.com/Snapmaker/OrcaSlicer, src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp), which
is AGPL-3.0-or-later. The catalog records facts about those settings, not
their code. packages/core/NOTICE says the same for the published package.

## Filament color data

Filament color names used for display (packages/core) were compiled from
Bambu Lab's and Polymaker's own published documentation and product pages
(filament names and hex color codes), not copied from any single vendor's
software. "Bambu," "Polymaker," and "Panchroma" are trademarks of their
respective owners, referenced here only to accurately name real,
publicly-sold filament colors; any2orca is not affiliated with, endorsed by,
or sponsored by any of them.

## Fonts (apps/web)

apps/web bundles the Inter and JetBrains Mono typefaces (apps/web/public/fonts/),
both licensed under the SIL Open Font License 1.1. Their license texts ship
alongside the font files: Inter-OFL.txt (Copyright 2016 The Inter Project
Authors) and JetBrainsMono-OFL.txt (Copyright 2020 The JetBrains Mono Project
Authors).

## Third-party code in the web app's bundle (apps/web)

The built site includes the runtime of Svelte, and the library's own
dependencies fflate and zod, all under the MIT license. Their license texts
are generated into the build as /third-party-licenses.txt (see
apps/web/scripts/copy-licenses.mjs), so the notices travel with every copy of
the site, including the tarball attached to each release.

## Icons (apps/web)

Most interface icons in the web app are from, or adapted from, Feather
(feather-icons 4.29.2, MIT, Copyright (c) 2013-2023 Cole Bemis); its license
text is in the generated /third-party-licenses.txt. The arrow logo is
any2orca's own. The GitHub mark, used only to link to the source repository,
is GitHub's.
